  "comments": "<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Non-magnetic (bronze) set issues (see link below):</span><br /><br />\r\nIn 1999, the Brilliant Uncirculated and Proof Annual sets featured pennies struck using bronze planchets, due to a world shortage of steel.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reports have been received regarding differing number of beads to both sides:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">1998-1999</span> 115 beads on obverse and 113 beads on reverse;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2000-2008</span> 110 beads on obverse and 109 beads on reverse;<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5c613e702cfd9.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5c613e702cfd9.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"169\" height=\"250\" /></a><br />\r\n© Heligal<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reports have also been received regarding reverse varieties for the 2000 &amp; 2004 issues:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2000</span> 1 points to left of dot;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">2004</span> 1 points to right of dot;<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5a97322330441.png\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5a97322330441.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n(former Spink ref. 4710)",
